 "_about": "How names and recurring terms are written in this language. Every translation follows this file, so a name is always spelled the same way. Names are written by sound, never translated (the author's rule). The spellings here are first versions based on the written names: the author's own pronunciation is recorded in Legacy/Behind The Scenes/World Lore/Word Pronunciation/Unique Words Pronounciation.wav, so correct any spelling here and later translations will follow it. Add new names the first time they are translated.",
 "rule": "Story names in Devanagari, by sound (हैरी, सनबी, फ़ॉरवे, बुरेज़). This covers coined world terms written as names too: creatures, plants, nari gels, spells, factions, guilds, ranks and coins (Bleed Out = ब्लीड आउट, Red Winga = रेड विंगा, Sapphire = सफ़ायर). Nari is written नरी, not नारी, because नारी means 'woman' in Hindi. A few descriptive place and object names whose plain meaning matters are translated (Nari Stones = नरी पत्थर, Black Honey = काला शहद, Bone Wood = हड्डी-लकड़ी, Blood Book = रक्त-ग्रंथ). The reader is addressed as तुम; sentences end with ।; digits are Western. The currency balls is गेंदें (sing. गेंद; सफ़ायर गेंद); the 'balls' double meaning is lost, so lines about courage use जिगरा. The unit timehunk is टाइमहंक; A.G. and B.G. stay in Latin letters. Real people (Deovandski, Deo, Mitsukiven, Mitsuken, Feiourm), the title and pets named in the afterwords (Peeta) stay in Latin letters. Logogram verb names drawn on the images (Transmute, Entangle, Right, Up...) stay in Latin letters. 'Sanbi shit!' (the Sanbi oath) is always बूढ़ी सनबी आत्मा! ('Old Sanbi soul!'), the author's rule.",
